--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WHAT THE WEB PAGE IS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WebhooksPage.tsx is a thin promotion wrapper: it sets a PageContainer (title,
subtitle, copyLink) and embeds <WebhookChannelsSection /> verbatim, so the
custom outgoing-webhook channels surface — HMAC-signed payloads, the four
persisted fields (name, URL, HTTP method, signing secret), the live
X-TeslaSync-Signature preview, per-row Test/Edit/Delete, and the recent delivery
audit — lives at /notifications/webhooks with a real page title/breadcrumb
instead of being a sub-section inside Settings. The page itself declares no data
of its own (the parity manifest records zero dataSources, zero panels, and
exactly two strings — requiredCount=2); the embedded WebhookChannelsSection owns
the kind=webhook feed (useWebhookChannels) plus the mutations (useSaveChannel /
useDeleteChannel / useToggleChannel / useTestWebhookChannel /
useWebhookSignaturePreview).

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
NATIVE IMPLEMENTATION (no placeholders, ADR-011; no delegation)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The shared A3 WebhookChannelsSection feature-view already exists
(io.teslasync.android.featureviews.webhookchannelssection.WebhookChannelsSection)
and owns every data state for its cache-then-network webhook feed: the row
skeleton chrome, the friendly no-webhooks empty state, the hard-error + retry
surface, the populated rows with their status pill + method chip + per-row
toggle/test/edit/delete, the stale/offline "last known" freshness chip with
auto-refresh, the add affordance, the create/edit modal (name, URL, method,
signing secret) with the live HMAC signature preview, the delete confirmation,
the inline structured test result, and the payload-variables doc box. This page
is its host: it sets the PageContainer-equivalent header and embeds the feature
view — never re-implementing it (DRY, ADR-006). This mirrors the sibling
notifications/ChannelsPage (also a 2-string wrapper that embeds the shared
NotificationChannelsView feature view) and notifications/ArchivedPage.

New files (package io.teslasync.android.notifications.webhooks):
  - WebhooksPageModel.kt   Registration(ROUTE_ID notificationsWebhooks,
                           WEB_PATH /notifications/webhooks, SLUG WebhooksPage)
                           + recordWebhooksPageOpened (the one PII-safe
                           view.opened diagnostic, P1/S11). No page-level feed —
                           the embedded feature view owns the webhook data.
  - WebhooksPage.kt        Stateful entry WebhooksPage(source, logger): records
                           view.opened, builds the feature view's
                           WebhookChannelsSectionViewModel via
                           viewModel(key=SLUG, factory=WebhookChannelsSectionView
                           Model.factory(source, logger)); stateless
                           WebhooksPageContent (verticalScroll Column: header +
                           WebhookChannelsSection) + WebhooksPageHeader (PageTitle
                           + subtitle BodyText + copy-link IconButton writing
                           WEB_PATH to the clipboard).
  - WebhooksPageHost.kt    WebhooksRoute() resolves LocalDataContainer, builds
                           the feature view source over
                           HttpNotificationChannelsRepository (filtered webhook
                           read + HMAC test + signature preview) +
                           HttpNotificationsRepository (channel CRUD), both on the
                           shared resilient client + offline cache, via
                           webhookChannelsSectionSource(channelsRepository=…,
                           notificationsRepository=…); WebhooksPageHost.register()
                           -> PageHosts.register("notificationsWebhooks").
                           Idempotent.

Edits (registration + string catalog + ledger only):
